    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Millersburg was originally the name of a Southern Pacific railroad station named for a local farming family.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millersburg%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The locale of Sugar Grove was renamed Millersburg to honor the work and services provided by the Millers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.millersburgoregon.gov/1439/Millersburg-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Millersburg incorporated in 1974 to prevent the city of Albany from extending its limits to include a zirconium processing plant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millersburg%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city's largest employer is a zirconium processing plant originally operated for the United States Bureau of Mines.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millersburg%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Millersburg is home to several industrial sites, including a titanium manufacturer and an industrial wood plant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
